From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:07:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: resume the connect cycle when a BSS socket of a
 connected manager terminates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

hostapd can remove and recreate a BSS that pWHM did not ask for: an AP MLD
partner link is parked while the owner of its driver context is re-added,
and comes back one second later under the same control socket name. The
AP-DISABLED on the link socket resets the MLD link ID of that VAP and
removes its AffiliatedAP entry, as for any BSS that goes away. Nothing
re-adopts it afterwards: the manager only restarts its connect cycle when
its last ready interface terminates, wld_wpaCtrlMngr_connect() is a no-op
while any interface is ready, hostapd sends AP-ENABLED for the first BSS of
an interface only, and a link adds no netdev. When the SYNC_STATE refresh
later found such a socket it re-opened it directly, without the manager
scan, so the link identity and the VAP state were never refreshed.

On a Wi-Fi 7 three-radio target this leaves Device.WiFi.APMLD.*.
AffiliatedAPNumberOfEntries at 2 (or 1) and the re-added link
AccessPoints Disabled while the driver beacons all three links, after
moving one AccessPoint out of and back into its MLD.

Resume the manager connect cycle from the TERMINATING handler when the
manager stays connected, its interface is still enabled and its daemon is
still enabled. The cycle rescans until every enabled interface is back or
the retry budget (20 x 500 ms) is spent; the scan re-adopts the MLD link
identity through the plugin socket resolver, re-attaches, and reports the
manager ready, which refreshes the radio and VAP states. Let the SYNC_STATE
refresh of a not-ready VAP socket go through the same cycle instead of a
bare open. A VAP that pWHM disables itself has its interface disabled
before the removal and arms nothing; the last-interface path is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c |  7 ++++++-
 src/nl80211/wld_wpaCtrl_events.c   | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c
@@ -745,7 +745,12 @@ void wifiGen_refreshVapsIfIdx(T_Radio* pRad) {
                (wld_hostapd_ap_needWpaCtrlIface(pAP)) &&
                (wld_wpaCtrlInterface_checkConnectionPath(pAP->wpaCtrlInterface)) &&
                (!wld_wpaCtrlInterface_isReady(pAP->wpaCtrlInterface))) {
-                wld_wpaCtrlInterface_open(pAP->wpaCtrlInterface);
+                /*
+                 * Re-attach through the manager connect cycle, not with a bare
+                 * open: only the manager scan re-adopts the MLD link identity of
+                 * a recreated link socket and refreshes the VAP state afterwards.
+                 */
+                wld_wpaCtrlMngr_resumeConnect(wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getMgr(pAP->wpaCtrlInterface), 0);
             }
         }
     }
diff --git a/src/nl80211/wld_wpaCtrl_events.c b/src/nl80211/wld_wpaCtrl_events.c
--- a/src/nl80211/wld_wpaCtrl_events.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_wpaCtrl_events.c
@@ -568,11 +568,30 @@ static void s_ifaceTerminatingEvt(wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pInterface, char* even
         return;
     }
     SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "%s: %s", pInterface->name, event);
-    bool isMgrTerm = (pInterface->isReady && (wld_wpaCtrlMngr_countReadyInterfaces(pInterface->pMgr) == 1));
+    wld_wpaCtrlMngr_t* pMgr = pInterface->pMgr;
+    bool isMgrTerm = (pInterface->isReady && (wld_wpaCtrlMngr_countReadyInterfaces(pMgr) == 1));
     pInterface->isReady = false;
     wld_wpaCtrlInterface_reset(pInterface);
     if(isMgrTerm) {
         CALL_MGR_I(pInterface, fMngrReadyCb, false);
+        return;
+    }
+    /*
+     * One BSS of a manager that stays connected went away while its daemon is
+     * still enabled. hostapd can bring such a BSS back on its own (an AP MLD
+     * partner parked while the owner of its driver context is re-added), under
+     * the same socket name and without any event this client still receives:
+     * no AP-ENABLED for a non-first BSS, no netdev for a link. Resume the
+     * connect cycle: its scan re-adopts the socket, the MLD link identity and,
+     * once every enabled interface is back, the VAP states, or it gives up
+     * after the usual retry budget.
+     */
+    if(wld_wpaCtrlInterface_isEnabled(pInterface) &&
+       wld_secDmn_isEnabled(pMgr->pSecDmn) &&
+       !wld_wpaCtrlMngr_isReady(pMgr)) {
+        SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "%s: manager stays connected: resume connect cycle to re-adopt the socket",
+                           pInterface->name);
+        wld_wpaCtrlMngr_resumeConnect(pMgr, RETRY_DELAY_MS);
     }
 }
 
